  was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one
  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Compiler.Semantics.adam - Adam's rules, results into the AST

  ResolveNames  every name of every module resolved once (BNF sec 1): a
                bare name, a dotted name A.B.C.X, a named type. The result
                is written into the AST (ResolvedDecl: the declaration a
                name means; ResolvedUnit: the unit a dotted prefix names)
                and read by every later phase, never re-derived.

  A bare name, in this order (BNF sec 1): the module's own scopes, the
  innermost first, each declaration before the use; the system scope (an
  intrinsic or builtin type wins over an import's export); an own name
  declared later (SM0002, still resolved); the imports, the LAST unit of
  the clause that exports it winning (not transitive); the runtime's public
  names (System.Runtime, in scope with no import, as Delphi's System unit);
  a bare choice value (SM0015); a member of the enclosing method's type (SM0018); else SM0021.

  A dotted name: a name its first part spells is that name (its members are
  M1.9's); else the LONGEST dotted prefix naming a unit of the import clause
  is the unit (ResolvedUnit on that prefix's node) and the next part its
  public member (SM0005 none, SM0006 not public); else SM0007 / SM0021.

  Also: a name used in its own var / const declaration (SM0001); a name
  declared twice in one scope (SM0004; overloads and a forward with its
  declaration excepted). Directive arguments are values of the directive,
  not names (left alone).

  CheckTypes    every expression, declaration and conversion of every module
                typed once (BNF sec 4, 6, 7), after ResolveNames. The type
                rule itself is Adam.Compiler.Types'. Written into the AST: an
                expression's and a declaration's ResolvedType, a value's
                ResolvedConvert where it goes to another type (no hidden
                conversions: only what the rule allows, a constant that fits,
                a literal's type-driven form), a member's ResolvedDecl (and
                the embed it is reached through in ResolvedEmbed), the loop,
                match or routine a leave, skip or return leaves in
                ResolvedJump, the init an object is built by in the builder's
                ResolvedCallee. The object family is checked here too (M1.9b):
                objects' virtual words, implements and embeds, is / as,
                own / ref / weak, inits' arguments, hidden members,
                properties' writes, const methods; a record's or an object's
                declared operators (SM0380-SM0386) and the binary / unary
                expressions that run one (the operator in their
                ResolvedDecl; SM0430 / SM0431). A string / char literal's
                fault in the encoding its type picked is reported last
                (SM0022 / SM0023).

  M1.10: every expression is folded as it is typed (Adam.Compiler.Folding:
  ResolvedConst, read by every fit check above it; a const's value in its
  type, choice values numbered as their list is typed; static array and set
  bounds first, so a type's key reads their values). A call of an overload
  set runs the member that takes its arguments by Adam's conversions and is
  better than every other by C++'s ranks (BNF sec 3; SM0402 none, SM0403
  none best; DoBuild's fit test), written as the callee's ResolvedDecl; two
  routines of one name with the same parameter types are SM0324. Layouts
  and vtable slots are Adam.Compiler.Layout's (CheckLayouts), linkage and
  symbols Adam.Compiler.Symbols' (NameSymbols), both run after CheckTypes.
  An unknown type (0) is silent: it was reported where it was lost, nothing
  cascades from it.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Compiler.Semantics;

import System.SysUtils, System.IO, Adam.Core.Common, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Core.Messages,
  Adam.Target, Adam.Compiler.SourceText, Adam.Compiler.SourceFiles, Adam.Compiler.Diagnostics, Adam.Compiler.Literals,
  Adam.Compiler.AST, Adam.Compiler.Scopes, Adam.Compiler.Types, Adam.Compiler.Layout,
  Adam.Compiler.Folding, Adam.Compiler.Formats, System.ResData;

public const
  // The runtime unit's routines Semantics writes into the AST (DESIGN sec 8): the text
  // writer print / println / FormatStr run (a print sink's, M3.8f2b), the exit an exe's block ends with, the heap's and the
  // arguments' that getmem / resizemem / freemem / paramcount / paramstr run
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_WRITE: string = "SinkText";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_EXIT: string = "ExitProgram";
  // The runtime's public exit code (BNF sec 5, M8h): an exe body's `return E;` stores into it
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_EXIT_CODE: string = "ExitCode";
  // The loader's event a dll's entry hands on (M8a): true when the dll's start is to run
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_DLL_EVENT: string = "DLLEvent";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_GETMEM: string = "GetMem";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_RESIZEMEM: string = "ResizeMem";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_FREEMEM: string = "FreeMem";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_PARAMCOUNT: string = "ParamCount";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_PARAMSTR: string = "ParamStr";
  // The path directives Semantics checks (DoDirectiveFiles): @exeicon / @copydll one
  // extension each and their file there, @addresdata's file there, the two search
  // folders there
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_ICON: string = "@exeicon";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_COPYDLL: string = "@copydll";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_RESDATA: string = "@addresdata";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_LIBRARYPATH: string = "@addlibrarypath";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_MODULEPATH: string = "@addmodulepath";
  // @message (DoMessages) and the severity words it takes (the parser checked them: PR0007)
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_DIRECTIVE_MESSAGE: string = "@message";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_MESSAGE_HINT: string = "hint";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_MESSAGE_WARN: string = "warn";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_MESSAGE_ERROR: string = "error";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_RAISE: string = "Raise";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_RAISECODE: string = "RaiseCode";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_EXCCODE: string = "ExcCode";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_EXCMSG: string = "ExcMsg";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_PROJECT_PASSWORD: string = "ProjectPassword";
  // The managed types' routines no node names (AST RuntimeRoutine, DoRuntimeRoutines)
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_STR_RELEASE: string = "StrRelease";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_STR_ASSIGN: string = "StrAssign";
  ADAM_SEMANTICS_RUNTIME_STR_WRITE: string = "SinkStr";
